# Unity C# practices

Detail: `docs/architecture/unity-coding.md`. Product code → `Assets/_Project/**` only.

## Structure

- Namespaces: `SmartElectric.*` (`Domain`, `AR`, `Adapters`, `UI`). One type per file; PascalCase types/methods, camelCase locals.
- Domain: **no** `MonoBehaviour`, **no** AR/UI APIs. Serializable POCOs / plain services. Optional asmdef later.
- MonoBehaviours = thin: wire scene refs, forward to Domain/services.
- `[SerializeField] private` for Inspector; avoid public fields. Require refs in `Awake`/`OnEnable` (fail fast if missing).

## Lifecycle & perf (mobile AR)

- Cache components in `Awake`; no `GetComponent` / `Find*` / `Camera.main` in `Update`.
- No LINQ / boxing / `new` lists in `Update`/`LateUpdate` hot paths.
- Prefer events / Input System callbacks over polling when possible.
- Stop coroutines / unsubscribe in `OnDisable`/`OnDestroy`.

## Unity hygiene

- Commit `.meta` with every asset/script. Don’t hand-edit GUIDs.
- Prefabs + scenes for wiring; runtime `AddComponent` only when justified.
- Input System (not legacy `Input`). Ask before new packages.
- Logs: temporary `Debug.Log` ok; don’t spam per-frame. No empty `catch`.
- Match existing style in `_Project`; don’t “clean up” template Samples unless asked.
